<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Trollheimen Triangle — Gjevilvasshytta–Jøldalshytta–Geithøtta–Trollheimshytta–Riarskaret summer triangle [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Walk the three-to-four-day Trollheimen circuit from Gjevilvasshytta to Jøldalshytta, over Geithøtta to Trollheimshytta, then via Riarskaret and Mellomfjellet back to Gjevilvasshytta. The approximately 58.5 km route crosses valleys, birch woods, lakes and high passes. Expect long rocky and boggy stages; the Riars stage is particularly strenuous. Use dry, snow-free summer conditions, confirm every bridge and required leg, and arrange hut accommodation separately. Gravbekken bridge rails are removed in winter. Do not substitute the harder Trollhetta summit traverse. Carry a map and compass, suitable footwear, warm and waterproof clothing, food and drinking water, and allow enough daylight for each stage.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright. Open Database License 1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/. Whole sources: https://www.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/relation/5482065/full (TNM6), https://www.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/relation/5484087/full (TNM12 via Geithøtta), and https://www.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/relation/5482064/full (TNM5 via Riarskaret and Mellomfjellet). Changes: whole original OSM road/path source intervals ordered and reversed only at literal shared nodes to form the closed hut circuit; canonical display simplified with the existing source-vertex helper. No coordinate snapping, synthetic connectors, private operator-track donation or elevation assignment. Descriptive planning geometry; not navigation-grade.

